🧠 Employee Data Analyzer (HR Dashboard using Python)
📌 Project Overview

The Employee Data Analyzer is a Python-based HR analytics dashboard that helps visualize and understand workforce data. It processes employee records from a CSV file and generates useful insights such as salary trends, department distribution, gender ratio, and performance patterns.
This project demonstrates how Python can be used for data-driven decision-making in HR using tools like Pandas, Matplotlib, and Seaborn.

⚙️ Tech Stack

Language: Python

Libraries: pandas, numpy, matplotlib, seaborn

Data Format: CSV

🔍 Key Features

✅ Load and clean HR data (CSV)
✅ Department-wise employee count
✅ Average salary analysis by department
✅ Gender distribution visualization
✅ Age vs Salary scatter analysis
✅ Correlation heatmap of employee metrics
✅ Top 10 highest-paid employees
✅ Experience vs Salary trend line

📊 Output Visuals

Bar charts for salary and department analysis

Pie chart for gender ratio

Heatmap for correlation

Scatter and line plots for relationship trends

💡 Insights Generated

Identify departments with the highest salaries

Observe how experience affects pay

Compare performance metrics across teams

Discover correlations between age, salary, and experience

🧩 How to Run

Place your dataset file as advanced_employee_data.csv in the same folder.

Run the Jupyter Notebook or Python script.

All charts and insights will be displayed automatically.

🏁 Project Goals

To help HR teams and data analysts make better workforce decisions through visual insights.
This project can be extended with predictive analytics and AI-based attrition analysis.
